## Rate Limiting Considerations

### Add Rate Limiting for Heavy Operations
```python
from django.views.decorators.cache import cache_page
from django.core.cache import cache

def rate_limited_endpoint(request):
    user_key = f"api_limit_{request.user.id}"
    current_requests = cache.get(user_key, 0)
    
    if current_requests >= 100:  # Max 100 requests per hour
        return JsonResponse({'status': 'error', 'message': 'Rate limit exceeded'})
    
    cache.set(user_key, current_requests + 1, 3600)  # 1 hour timeout
```